# Chrony configuration for a client of this box. Drop-in; no `prefer`.
#
# The box is a stratum-1 GPS reference one cable away, and it beats a pool by
# four orders of magnitude of distance while it is sane. It has also returned
# 134 ms of confidently-wrong time for two and a half hours while claiming
# 2.4 us, so it must be able to lose. Without `prefer`, chrony ranks on distance
# and does exactly that within minutes; with `prefer` it keeps taking it.
#
# Named, not addressed: the box holds a static DHCP reservation, so the name
# survives an address change instead of the client going quietly stale. The
# suffix is left off and comes from the resolver's search domain; write it in
# full on a client that has none.
#
# Internet sources stay as the fallback for a reboot, a lost fix or a dead box.
# chrony needs no mark removed to switch back.

server esp32p4-ntp iburst minpoll 4 maxpoll 6

# Fallbacks. minpoll 5 is 32 s, which is plenty for a source that should rarely
# be needed.
pool 2.debian.pool.ntp.org iburst minpoll 5 maxpoll 7
server time.cloudflare.com iburst minpoll 5 maxpoll 7
server time.apple.com      iburst minpoll 5 maxpoll 7

# Step only for gross errors: a jump of a second is a fault, not drift, and
# slewing it would take twenty minutes.
makestep 1.0 3

# Never trust a source that claims more than this.
maxdistance 16.0

driftfile /var/lib/chrony/chrony.drift
